## Output format

Respond with a single JSON object — no prose before or after, no markdown fences are required but are tolerated.  Exactly this shape:

```json
{
  "decision": "write",
  "reasoning": "One or two sentences explaining whether this passes the gating bar and why.",
  "memory": {
    "title": "Short, specific title — ideally unique and greppable.",
    "kind": "fact | rule | lesson",
    "scope": "charm | global",
    "body": "A concise Markdown body.  A few bullets or sentences — not a wall of text.  Include the trigger's concrete symptom, the resolution, and any pitfalls for next time.",
    "tags": ["optional", "short", "tags"]
  }
}
```

When the event does not pass the bar, respond with:

```json
{
  "decision": "skip",
  "reasoning": "One sentence explaining why it is not worth remembering."
}
```

Be ruthless — most events should `skip`.  Only write when you can answer the "saves five minutes" question with a concrete scenario.
